s can determine","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:9d3cc4f4165bfe868dde771afa4469d569574ff8d3d506b70d75f97f505da643","file":"preprints/From-partial-permutation-information-to-Fourier-bounds-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":18,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"ea2f106b4b1ac6e3593db7f730f401596e2c7133a9b83c240ac4769f07d9f3fd","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/From-partial-permutation-information-to-Fourier-bounds-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9d3cc4f4165bfe868dde771afa4469d569574ff8d3d506b70d75f97f505da643","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/From-partial-permutation-information-to-Fourier-bounds-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L18"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{l:main}\nPartition $X$ into $b$ nonempty sets $M_1,\\ldots,M_b$. Put $H_i=H_{M_i}$. Suppose $f$ is a nonnegative measure on $G$ of mass at most one and, for every $g\\in G$ and $i$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{l:main-cap}\n f(gH_i)\\le \\frac{B}{[G:H_i]}.\n\\end{equation}\nFor every $u>0$ and every irreducible $\\rho$ of degree $D$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{l:main-hs}\n \\|\\widehat f(\\rho)\\|_{\\HS}^2\n \\le bBC_uD^{-1+(u+2)/b}.\n\\end{equation}\nThere is also an independent orbit-span proof of the bound\n\\begin{equation}\\label{l:main-orbit}\n \\|\\widehat f(\\rho)\\|_{\\op}^2\n \\le bBC_uD^{-1+(u+2)/b}.\n\\end{equation}\nNo restriction is imposed on block sizes or on the multiplicities in $\\rho|_{H_1\\times\\cdots\\times H_b}$."}
